<title>UK: Marley says has good start to current year.</title>
<headline>Marley says has good start to current year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British building products group Marley Plc said on Thursday its current year had started well, with UK profits improving as a result of higher volumes and prices in housebuilding.</p>
<p>&quot;UK profits are improving as new housebuilding activity has increased through the spring,&quot; chairman Sir George Russell told the company's annual meeting.</p>
<p>Russell said the group's overseas earnings were still on a rising trend despite the adverse impact from high sterling exchange rates.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
